# Personal recordings and exports, added in 7.0.
# Video upload mode means clips of real faces now get dragged near this
# folder, and an exported CSV is measurements of somebody's eyes. Both
# are personal data, this repository is public, and git history keeps a
# file even after a later commit deletes it. So they are refused at the
# door rather than cleaned up afterwards.
*.mp4
*.webm
*.mov
*.avi
*.mkv
blinklab-session-*.csv
recordings/
